        <title type="html"><![CDATA[docs: clarify onevent and addEventListener interaction behaviour]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40799</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40799"/>
        <updated>2025-08-19T15:41:33.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91039605?u=75d9215ac93cf8524615e7259f3f7ec619bc564e&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description (<a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3328690490" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40767" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/40767/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40767">#40767</a>)</h3>
<p dir="auto">Hello,<br>
The MDN documentation was missing crucial info about what happens when you mix different ways of adding event listeners to the same element.<br>
I have expanded the "Using onevent properties" section to explain how they Interact, across six different scenarios and some important details like how stopImmediatePropagation() affects the order, and that options like once and passive only work with addEventListener().</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">To prevent developers from wasting hours debugging event handler conflicts.</p>]]></content>
